// Ore processing's handbook texts that quote the pack's figures (lang/en.json), each with {{name}}
// where a figure goes. make_ore_guide_numbers.py (beside this) fills them from config/ore-processing.json
// and a few C# constants and writes them into en.json; its figures() names every placeholder.
// Edit these texts here, never in en.json, then run
//   python3 mods-src/seraphhorizons/Ore/tools/make_ore_guide_numbers.py
// tools/tests/test_ore_guide_numbers.py fails CI when en.json and this drift apart.
{
  "oreprocessing-rawore-sulfide-handbook-text": "A sulfide: its metal is bound to sulfur, and it does not smelt as it is. Roast it in a firepit on any fuel, at about {{roastPoint}} °C, into roasted ore, which smelts at its grade's share less what the fire loses (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreroasting\">Roasting sulfide ore</a>); or crush and concentrate it, which keeps far more (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>). Set it down on the ground and strike it with a hammer to break it into crushed ore (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-spalling\">Spalling ore</a>).",
  "oreprocessing-guide-text": "Ore comes out of the ground as rock with metal in it, and every step from the rock face to the ingot either keeps that metal or loses some of it. This page is the whole line; each item's own page says what that item is for, and the guides linked below go into the steps. The figures are the pack's defaults.\n\n<strong>Grades, and smelting rock</strong>\nRaw ore holds metal by its grade: most ores {{rawUnits}} units a piece, poor to bountiful. A furnace has to slag the rock off, and metal goes with the slag, so rock (raw, crushed or ground ore alike) smelts at only a share of what it holds. A sulfide's roasted ore smelts at that share times what its roast kept:\n\n<strong>Poor</strong>: {{smelt.poor}} %; roasted in a firepit {{roasted.poor}} %, in the stall roaster {{stallRoasted.poor}} %\n<strong>Medium</strong>: {{smelt.medium}} %; roasted {{roasted.medium}} %, stall-roasted {{stallRoasted.medium}} %\n<strong>Rich</strong>: {{smelt.rich}} %; roasted {{roasted.rich}} %, stall-roasted {{stallRoasted.rich}} %\n<strong>Bountiful</strong>: {{smelt.bountiful}} %; roasted {{roasted.bountiful}} %, stall-roasted {{stallRoasted.bountiful}} %\n\nConcentrate, roasted concentrate and retorted sponge smelt whole: {{smeltWhole}} %. So concentrating is the step that keeps the metal: it throws the rock away before the furnace sees it.\n\n<strong>Crushing and grinding</strong>\nCrushing never loses metal: one raw ore breaks into one crushed ore of its grade (crystallised ore into two). By hand, set raw ore on the ground and strike it with a hammer (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-spalling\">Spalling ore</a>); the jaw breaker, the stamp battery and the pulverizer crush by power. Crushed ore smelts as the raw ore does; its worth is that the concentrators take it. Poor ore is fine-grained: grind it into ground ore on the arrastra or the ball mill, or the concentrators catch little of it. The quern grinds no ore.\nClassifying sorts crushed ore to an even size, which washes better: by hand shake it through the riddle (the oversize goes back to be spalled again); the stamp battery's and the ball mill's screens classify what they crush.\nRich gravel and bog iron are placer: their metal is already loose, so they are washed, never crushed or classified. Rich gravel goes to the gold pan, the rocker or the concentrators, bog iron to the concentrators only.\n\n<strong>Concentrating</strong>\nThe gold pan and the rocker by hand, and the sluice, jig, shaking table and vanner by water and power, wash the light rock away and keep the heavy grains as <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:concentrate-hematite\">concentrate</a>, {{concentrateUnits}} units of metal a piece. By hand the pan keeps {{pan}} % and the rocker {{rocker}} % of what they can catch, and what they miss is spent. The machines each catch their share of what the one before missed (the sluice {{sluice}} %, the jig {{jig}} %, the table {{table}} %, the vanner {{vanner}} %), so a full line keeps nearly all of it. Feed that was not classified, poor ore that was not ground and free gold or silver that was not amalgamated hold part of their metal out of reach.\nOre that went the whole way (classified, ground if poor, amalgamated if free, then the sluice, jig and table before the vanner) loses nothing at the end: for an oxide or a native metal the vanner keeps all that is left, and a sulfide's concentrate comes out of the reverberatory roaster whole. An ore with a second metal keeps only what the line caught, as smelting it to bullion does not carry that on.\n\n<strong>Roasting</strong>\nGalena, chalcopyrite, sphalerite and the other sulfides do not smelt as they are, raw, crushed, ground or concentrated: they are roasted first, which burns the sulfur off.\nIn a <a href=\"handbook://block-firepit-cold\">firepit</a>, on any fuel, at about {{roastPoint}} °C, raw and crushed sulfide ore roast one for one into roasted ore, and concentrate into <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-galena\">roasted concentrate</a>. Open roasting keeps {{firepit}} % of the metal: 20 concentrate roast to {{firepit.of20}}, and roasted ore smelts at its grade's share times {{firepit}} %.\nThe stall roaster takes a heap of raw or crushed rock at a time: stall-roasted ore smelts at its grade's share times {{stallroaster}} %, and {{stallroaster.sulfur}} of the sulfur comes back as sulfur powder.\nThe reverberatory roaster takes concentrate by chute and {{reverberatory.loses}}; {{reverberatory.sulfur}} % of the sulfur comes back.\nGround sulfide ore does not roast as rock: concentrate it first. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreroasting\">Roasting sulfide ore</a>.\n\n<strong>Amalgam and the still</strong>\nGold and silver quartz carry free metal that gravity alone partly misses. Mercury takes it up: the amalgam pan and the amalgamation plates catch it as <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:amalgam-quartz_nativegold\">amalgam</a>, which does not smelt. Retort the amalgam in the still (a boiler on a lit firepit with a condenser beside it): {{mercuryReturn}} of its mercury comes back, and the gold or silver stays behind as retorted sponge, which smelts whole. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreretorting\">Retorting mercury</a>.\n\n<strong>Bullion and parting</strong>\nSome ores carry a second metal, and every form of them smelts to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-galena-lead\">base bullion</a>: a bar of {{barUnits}} units of the first metal with the second still in it.\n<strong>Galena, argentiferous galena</strong>: silver-lead ({{byProduct.galena}} or {{byProduct.galena_nativesilver}} silver), parted in the cupellation furnace\n<strong>Tetrahedrite</strong>: argentiferous copper ({{byProduct.tetrahedrite}} silver), in the cupellation furnace with {{cupel.leadAdded}} lead added\n<strong>Freibergite</strong>: cupriferous silver ({{byProduct.freibergite}} copper), in the cupellation furnace with {{cupel.leadAdded}} lead added\n<strong>Teallite, franckeite</strong>: tin-lead ({{byProduct.teallite}} or {{byProduct.franckeite}} lead), in the liquation furnace\n<strong>Gold quartz</strong>: doré ({{byProduct.quartz_nativegold}} silver), in the acid parting vessel\nThe parting machines win the second metal at {{partingMachines}} %. Smelted again as it is, a bar gives its first metal (doré {{unparted.quartz_nativegold}} % of its gold) and the second is lost. By hand, the <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> parts the silver from roasted galena, tetrahedrite or freibergite concentrate, and the liquation pan the lead from roasted teallite or franckeite concentrate, at {{handParting}} % (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-liquation\">Liquation: tin from lead</a>). The guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> takes each kind through its parting, with what every machine gives.\n\n<strong>Rich lead and litharge</strong>\nPlain galena's silver-lead can go through the Parkes kettle first, which takes its silver out with zinc into <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:richlead\">rich lead</a>, lead {{richLeadSilver}} of which is silver; the cupellation furnace parts all of that silver. Cupellation burns the lead to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>, which smelts back to lead at a small loss, {{litharge.out}} to every {{litharge.in}}.\n\nThe pack's recipe browser has an Ore routes page that works these figures out for every ore and grade, by hand and by machine: <a href=\"https://benjamin-kirkbride.github.io/Seraph-Horizons/\">benjamin-kirkbride.github.io/Seraph-Horizons</a>.",
  "oreproduct-crushed-sulfide-handbook-text": "A sulfide's crushed ore does not smelt as it is. Roast it in a firepit at about {{roastPoint}} °C, or in the stall roaster, into roasted ore that smelts at its grade's share less what the roast loses (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreroasting\">Roasting sulfide ore</a>); or concentrate it and roast the concentrate, which keeps far more. Poor ore is fine-grained: grind it before the concentrators. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-roastedrock-handbook-text": "A sulfide's raw or crushed ore roasted in a firepit, its sulfur burned off. It smelts at its grade's share times the firepit's {{firepit}} %: open roasting loses the rest with the fumes, and a slot of rock is still a slot of rock, so concentrating first keeps far more. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreroasting\">Roasting sulfide ore</a> and <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-stallroastedrock-handbook-text": "A sulfide's raw or crushed ore roasted in the stall roaster, its sulfur burned off. It smelts at its grade's share times the stall's {{stallroaster}} %, where the firepit's roasted ore keeps {{firepit}} %. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-concentrate-handbook-text": "The heavy grains a concentrator keeps, the rock thrown away: {{concentrateUnits}} units of metal a piece, which smelt whole in any furnace. A sulfide's concentrate (galena, chalcopyrite, sphalerite and the rest) does not smelt until roasted: in a firepit, on any fuel at about {{roastPoint}} °C, one at a time, {{firepit}} % of its metal comes out in the roasted concentrate; the reverberatory roaster {{reverberatory.keeps}}. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreroasting\">Roasting sulfide ore</a> and <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-amalgam-handbook-text": "Free gold or silver caught in mercury, on the amalgam pan or the amalgamation plates. It does not smelt: retort it in the still (a boiler on a lit firepit with a condenser beside it), which gives back {{mercuryReturn}} of the mercury and leaves the gold or silver as sponge (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreretorting\">Retorting mercury</a>). See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-litharge-handbook-text": "Lead oxide: the lead a cupel or the cupellation furnace burns off its charge. It smelts back to lead at a small loss, {{litharge.out}} to every {{litharge.in}}. See <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a>.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-galena-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-galena-shale\">galena</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of lead carrying {{byProduct.galena}} units of silver. Only parting gets the silver out.\n\n<strong>Parkes kettle, then cupellation</strong>\nThe best way. Charge the <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:parkeskettle-north\">Parkes kettle</a> with up to {{parkeskettle.bars}} bars and stir in zinc bits, a unit of zinc to {{parkeskettle.leadPerZinc}} of lead ({{parkeskettle.zincBits}} bits to a full charge). A full charge gives {{parkeskettle.richBars}} bars of <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:richlead\">rich lead</a> ({{richLead.silver}} silver each), {{parkeskettle.leadIngots}} lead ingots and {{parkeskettle.zincBack}} zinc bits back; the {{parkeskettle.silverCarried}} units of silver short of another bar stay in the kettle for the next charge. The <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a> then parts all of rich lead's silver, so none of the ore's is lost.\n\n<strong>Cupellation alone</strong>\nThe cupellation furnace takes these bars directly too, {{cupellationfurnace.chargeBars}} to a charge: {{parted.galena}} units of silver a bar, the lead going to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>, which smelts back to lead at a small loss, {{litharge.out}} to every {{litharge.in}}.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nA <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> in the forge parts the silver from <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-galena\">roasted galena concentrate</a>, not from the bar: {{hand.galena}} units of silver to {{barUnits}} of lead.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of lead and the silver is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-galena_nativesilver-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-galena_nativesilver-shale\">argentiferous galena</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of lead carrying {{byProduct.galena_nativesilver}} units of silver, far richer than plain galena's {{byProduct.galena}}.\n\n<strong>Cupellation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:parkeskettle-north\">Parkes kettle</a> refuses it: it is already richer than the kettle's own <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:richlead\">rich lead</a> ({{richLead.silver}} silver to a bar). Take it straight to the <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a>, {{cupellationfurnace.chargeBars}} bars to a charge. A bar gives {{parted.galena_nativesilver}} units of silver; the lead goes to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>, which smelts back to lead at a small loss, {{litharge.out}} to every {{litharge.in}}.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nA <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> in the forge parts the silver from <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-galena_nativesilver\">roasted argentiferous galena concentrate</a>, not from the bar: {{hand.galena_nativesilver}} units of silver to {{barUnits}} of lead.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of lead and all its silver is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-tetrahedrite-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-tetrahedrite-gneiss\">tetrahedrite</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of copper carrying {{byProduct.tetrahedrite}} units of silver.\n\n<strong>Cupellation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a> parts it, but copper does not cupel on its own: charge as many lead ingots as bars, so a full charge is one bar and one lead ingot. The bar gives {{parted.tetrahedrite}} units of silver, and its copper comes back beside the silver, as bits; the lead goes to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nA <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> in the forge parts <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-tetrahedrite\">roasted tetrahedrite concentrate</a>, not the bar, with {{cupel.leadAdded}} lead added (lead bits or roasted galena): {{hand.tetrahedrite}} units of silver to {{barUnits}} of copper.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of copper and the silver is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-freibergite-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-freibergite-gneiss\">freibergite</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of silver carrying {{byProduct.freibergite}} units of copper.\n\n<strong>Cupellation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a> parts it with as many lead ingots as bars: a full charge is one bar and one lead ingot. The copper burns off with the lead and is won back beside the silver. A bar gives all its silver and {{parted.freibergite}} units of copper, both as bits; the lead goes to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nA <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> in the forge parts <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-freibergite\">roasted freibergite concentrate</a>, not the bar, with {{cupel.leadAdded}} lead added (lead bits or roasted galena): {{hand.freibergite}} units of copper to {{barUnits}} of silver.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of silver and the copper is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-teallite-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-teallite-claystone\">teallite</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of tin carrying {{byProduct.teallite}} units of lead.\n\n<strong>Liquation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationfurnace-north\">liquation furnace</a> takes up to {{liquationfurnace.chargeBars}} bars (mixed with franckeite's if you like) and sweats them at {{liquationfurnace.perHour}} units of tin an hour: tin melts long before lead, so the tin runs off into the pot and the lead stays on the plate. A bar gives all its tin and {{parted.teallite}} units of lead.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationpan-raw\">liquation pan</a> in a firepit or a forge parts <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-teallite\">roasted teallite concentrate</a>, not the bar: a full pan, {{liquationpan.concentrate}} concentrate, gives {{liquationpan.units}} units of tin and {{liquationpan.teallite}} of lead (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-liquation\">Liquation: tin from lead</a>).\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of tin and the lead is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-franckeite-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-franckeite-claystone\">franckeite</a> smelted in a crucible gives this bar: {{barUnits}} units of tin carrying {{byProduct.franckeite}} units of lead.\n\n<strong>Liquation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationfurnace-north\">liquation furnace</a> takes up to {{liquationfurnace.chargeBars}} bars (mixed with teallite's if you like) and sweats them at {{liquationfurnace.perHour}} units of tin an hour: tin melts long before lead, so the tin runs off into the pot and the lead stays on the plate. A bar gives all its tin and {{parted.franckeite}} units of lead.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationpan-raw\">liquation pan</a> in a firepit or a forge parts <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:roastedconcentrate-franckeite\">roasted franckeite concentrate</a>, not the bar: a full pan, {{liquationpan.concentrate}} concentrate, gives {{liquationpan.units}} units of tin and {{liquationpan.franckeite}} of lead (<a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-liquation\">Liquation: tin from lead</a>).\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of tin and the lead is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-bullion-quartz_nativegold-handbook-text": "Any form of <a href=\"handbook://item-ore-medium-quartz_nativegold-granite\">gold quartz</a> smelted in a crucible, its concentrate or the sponge from the still among them, gives doré: {{barUnits}} units of gold carrying {{byProduct.quartz_nativegold}} units of silver. Unlike the other bullion, it loses some of its own metal unparted.\n\n<strong>Acid parting</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:acidparting-north\">acid parting vessel</a> takes up to {{acidparting.chargeBars}} bars, with {{acidparting.acidPerBar}} litres of aqua fortis to a bar and a litre of wash water to every {{acidparting.unitsPerLitre}} units, and parts {{acidparting.perHour}} units an hour. All the gold comes out, {{barUnits}} units a bar, and {{parted.quartz_nativegold}} units of silver, thrown down on the copper plate in the tub.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nThere is no hand station for acid parting.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives only {{unparted.quartz_nativegold.units}} units of gold ({{unparted.quartz_nativegold}} %) and the silver is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreproduct-richlead-handbook-text": "The <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:parkeskettle-north\">Parkes kettle</a>'s zinc crust, retorted: a bar of {{barUnits}} units of lead carrying {{richLead.silver}} units of silver, {{richLeadSilver}} of its lead. The kettle makes it from <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-galena-lead\">plain galena's silver-lead</a>, gathering a whole charge's silver into a few bars: a full charge of {{parkeskettle.bars}} bars gives {{parkeskettle.richBars}}.\n\n<strong>Cupellation</strong>\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a> parts all of its silver, none lost: {{richLead.silver}} units a bar, {{cupellationfurnace.chargeBars}} bars to a charge, or mixed with other bullion it cupels, at {{cupellationfurnace.perHour}} units of lead an hour. The lead goes to <a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:litharge\">litharge</a>, which smelts back to lead at a small loss, {{litharge.out}} to every {{litharge.in}}.\n\n<strong>Remelted</strong>\nSmelted again as it is, a bar gives {{barUnits}} units of lead and the silver is lost.\n\nThe guide <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing-bullion\">Base bullion</a> sets the kinds side by side; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line.",
  "oreprocessing-bullion-text": "Some ores carry a second metal: galena and argentiferous galena silver, tetrahedrite silver, freibergite copper, teallite and franckeite lead, gold quartz silver. A crucible melts the two together, so every form of these ores that smelts (a sulfide once roasted) gives <strong>base bullion</strong> in a crucible: a bar of {{barUnits}} units of the ore's main metal with the second metal still in it, poured into an ingot mold like any metal. Bullion is made only in a crucible. Each kind's own page says how to part it; <a href=\"handbook://seraphhorizons-oreprocessing\">Ore processing</a> is the whole line from the rock face.\n\n<strong>The kinds</strong>\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-galena-lead\">Silver-lead</a> (galena): {{barUnits}} lead, {{byProduct.galena}} silver\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-galena_nativesilver-lead\">Silver-lead</a> (argentiferous galena): {{barUnits}} lead, {{byProduct.galena_nativesilver}} silver\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-tetrahedrite-copper\">Argentiferous copper</a> (tetrahedrite): {{barUnits}} copper, {{byProduct.tetrahedrite}} silver\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-freibergite-silver\">Cupriferous silver</a> (freibergite): {{barUnits}} silver, {{byProduct.freibergite}} copper\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-teallite-tin\">Tin-lead</a> (teallite): {{barUnits}} tin, {{byProduct.teallite}} lead\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-franckeite-tin\">Tin-lead</a> (franckeite): {{barUnits}} tin, {{byProduct.franckeite}} lead\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:bullion-quartz_nativegold-gold\">Doré</a> (gold quartz): {{barUnits}} gold, {{byProduct.quartz_nativegold}} silver\n<a href=\"handbook://item-seraphhorizons:richlead\">Rich lead</a> (the Parkes kettle's): {{barUnits}} lead, {{richLead.silver}} silver\n\n<strong>Parting</strong>\nA parting machine wins the second metal, at {{partingMachines}} %.\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupellationfurnace-north\">cupellation furnace</a>: silver-lead, argentiferous copper and cupriferous silver (the last two with as many lead ingots as bars), and rich lead, whose silver it parts whole.\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:parkeskettle-north\">Parkes kettle</a>: plain galena's silver-lead only, before the cupellation furnace. It gathers the silver into rich lead and the rest comes out as plain lead, so galena's silver comes out whole. Argentiferous galena's is already richer than the kettle's crust: cupel it directly.\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationfurnace-north\">liquation furnace</a>: tin-lead.\nThe <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:acidparting-north\">acid parting vessel</a>: doré, with aqua fortis.\n\n<strong>By hand</strong>\nThe hand stations part roasted concentrate, not bars, at {{handParting}} %: a <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:cupel-fired\">cupel</a> in the forge for galena, argentiferous galena, tetrahedrite and freibergite (the last two with {{cupel.leadAdded}} lead added), and the <a href=\"handbook://block-seraphhorizons:liquationpan-raw\">liquation pan</a> for teallite and franckeite. Doré has no hand station.\n\n<strong>Remelting</strong>\nBullion smelted again as it is gives its main metal and loses the second: a silver-lead bar gives {{barUnits}} units of lead and no silver. Doré loses more, giving only {{unparted.quartz_nativegold.units}} units of gold. Part it first."
}
